   "_dt": 1793862000.0,
   "ageDays": 0.06,
   "summary": "The scheme, approved on Wednesday, will support the development of 60 GWh of hydro pumped storage capacity, 30 GWh of battery energy storage systems and two GWh of alternative energy storage technologies, according to an official government statement. The initiative is also designed to strengthen India’s domestic energy storage manufacturing industry through financial support for local producers and reduce the country’s dependence on imported components.",
   "summary_zh": "据政府官方声明，该计划于周三获批，将支持开发60 GWh的抽水蓄能能力、30 GWh的电池储能系统以及2 GWh的替代能源储能技术。这项倡议还旨在通过向本土生产商提供财政支持来 strengthening 印度的国内储能制造业，并降低该国对进口零部件的依赖。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Sign in Welcome! Log into your account Forgot your password? Get help Password recovery Recover your password A password will be e-mailed to you. Thursday, November 5, 2026 Sign in / Join Facebook Instagram Linkedin Mail Spotify X Youtube Nigeria Africa World Business and Tech Politics Sports Languages Yoruba Igbo Hausa French Arabic Fulfulde Kiswahili Mandarin connect Home World World India Approves $1.53 Billion Energy Storage Scheme November 5, 2026 Share Facebook X Pinterest WhatsApp The Indian government has approved a 1.53-billion-dollar scheme to develop 92 gigawatt-hours (GWh) of energy storage capacity. The move aims to strengthen the country’s energy security and support its renewable energy expansion. The scheme, approved on Wednesday, will support the development of 60 GWh of hydro pumped storage capacity, 30 GWh of battery energy storage systems and two GWh of alternative energy storage technologies, according to an official government statement. The initiative is also designed to strengthen India’s domestic energy storage manufacturing industry through financial support for local producers and reduce the country’s dependence on imported components. Energy storage is considered crucial to managing the intermittent supply of renewable energy, particularly solar and wind power, by storing excess electricity for use when generation is low or demand is high. The investment comes as India pursues an ambitious target of achieving 500 gigawatts of non-fossil fuel-based electricity capacity by 2030. The government expects the scheme to encourage private-sector investment, promote technological development and improve the reliability of the country’s power supply as it transitions towards cleaner energy sources. ABOUT US (VON) is the state-owned international broadcasting station, established in 1961 to provide authoritative news and positive perspectives on Nigeria and Africa. Based in Abuja with headquarters and studio facilities in Lugbe, Abuja and Lagos, it broadcasts globally in 8 languages, including English, French, Arabic, and indigenous languages like Igbo, Yoruba, and Hausa",
