   "ageDays": 1.02,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Indian-American Vivek Ramaswamy, who was backed by U.S. President Donald Trump, lost Ohio's gubernatorial race to Democrat Amy Acton. Mr. Ramaswamy, 41, lost to 60-year-old Ms. Acton, who became the first woman to be elected Governor of the state. Mr. Ramaswamy, who made an unsuccessful bid against Trump for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024, pumped more than $36 million in loans from his personal fortune into the race, The Washington Post reported.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。获美国总统唐纳德·特朗普支持的印度裔美国人维杰克·拉马斯瓦米在俄亥俄州州长选举中败给民主党人艾米·阿克顿。41岁的拉马斯瓦米败给了60岁的阿克顿，后者成为该州首位当选州长的女性。《华盛顿邮报》报道，拉马斯瓦米曾在2024年竞选共和党总统候选人提名时挑战特朗普但未获成功，此次选举中他从个人财富中投入逾3600万美元贷款。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Indian-American Vivek Ramaswamy, who was backed by U.S. President Donald Trump, lost Ohio's gubernatorial race to Democrat Amy Acton. Mr. Ramaswamy, 41, lost to 60-year-old Ms. Acton, who became the first woman to be elected Governor of the state. Ms. Acton bagged over 51% of the votes while Mr. Ramaswamy won over 45%. In concession remarks in Ohio after losing the Governor's race, Mr. Ramaswamy said: \"It was a tough race. It was bitter at times in both directions... All of us in this room should be rooting for the success of her administration,\" C-SPAN quoted him as saying. The billionaire also thanked his parents, his wife and her parents for their support. Mr. Ramaswamy lost despite having top strategists from his and Vice President JD Vance’s political teams advising him, NBC News reported. Mr. Ramaswamy, who made an unsuccessful bid against Trump for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024, pumped more than $36 million in loans from his personal fortune into the race, The Washington Post reported. He also received millions of dollars in donations from fellow billionaires Elon Musk and Jeffrey Yass, NBC News reported. Days ahead of the election, Mr. Ramaswamy drew criticism for the decision to air an ad in which Acton’s mother, Donna Arthur, called her daughter a liar and urged Ohioans not to vote for her, the report said. Ms. Acton said she has not seen or spoken with Arthur in nearly 50 years and has accused her mother’s then-husband of sexually abusing her as a child, it said. Mr. Ramaswamy helped Elon Musk plan President Donald Trump’s Department of Government Efficiency initiative to overhaul the federal government. After quitting the post, Mr. Ramaswamy received an endorsement from Mr. Trump. The President travelled to Ohio to lend his support to Mr. Ramaswamy. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
