   "title": "Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets",
   "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets",
   "domain": "france24.com",
   "source": "france24.com",
   "published": "Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:21:19 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793719279.0,
   "ageDays": 1.71,
   "summary": "Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre.",
   "summary_zh": "愤怒长期以来一直是推动政治变革的力量，但随着美国中期选举临近以及法国持续爆发抗议活动，两国广泛存在的愤怒情绪如今成为最突出的议题。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract",
