   "_dt": 1793673723.0,
   "ageDays": 2.23,
   "summary": "Korean stocks traded more than 2 percent lower late Tuesday morning, led by tech losses amid lingering woes about the excessive pace of artificial intelligence (AI) spending. Opening 2.46 percent lower, the benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) fell 145.02 points, or 2.48 percent, to 5,714.06 as of 11:20 a.m. Overnight on Wall Street, the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite and the S&P 500 closed 1.07 percent and 0.51 percent lower, respectively, ahead of the U.S. midterm elections slated for Tuesday.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国股市周二上午晚盘交易下跌逾2%，科技股领跌，市场仍担忧人工智能（AI）支出增长过快。截至上午11时20分，韩国综合股价指数（KOSPI）开盘下跌2.46%，随后下跌145.02点，跌幅2.48%，报5,714.06点。前一交易时段，华尔街科技股占比居前的纳斯达克综合指数和标准普尔500指数分别收跌1.07%和0.51%，美国中期选举则定于周二举行。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korean stocks traded more than 2 percent lower late Tuesday morning, led by tech losses amid lingering woes about the excessive pace of artificial intelligence (AI) spending. Opening 2.46 percent lower, the benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) fell 145.02 points, or 2.48 percent, to 5,714.06 as of 11:20 a.m. Overnight on Wall Street, the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite and the S&P 500 closed 1.07 percent and 0.51 percent lower, respectively, ahead of the U.S. midterm elections slated for Tuesday. Investor sentiment was dampened by concerns that massive spending on AI infrastructure is undermining tech firms' near-term profitability. Market bellwether Samsung Electronics sank 2.95 percent, and its chipmaking rival SK hynix slid 3.8 percent. Hanmi Semiconductor, a leading chip equipment maker, fell 4.17 percent, and SK Square, the parent of SK hynix, tumbled 4 percent. Steel giant POSCO Holdings slumped 5.3 percent, and leading oil refinery SK Innovation plunged 7.76 percent. The Korean won was trading at 1,341 won against the U.S. dollar as of 11:20 a.m., up 3.4 won from the previous session's close",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
