   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 11:47:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793620022.0,
   "ageDays": 2.86,
   "summary": "Korea will hold an annual consultation session with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) this week to discuss the country's overall economic situation and policies, the finance ministry said Monday. An IMF delegation, led by mission chief Corinne Delechat, is scheduled to have meetings with government ministries, including the finance, budget and industry ministries, the Bank of Korea (BOK) and other public and private institutions, according to the Ministry of Finance and Economy.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国财政部周一表示，本周将与国际货币基金组织（IMF）举行年度磋商会议，讨论韩国整体经济状况及政策。韩国财政经济部称，由IMFmission首席代表科琳·德勒沙率领的代表团将与韩国财政部、预算部、产业部、韩国银行（BOK）及其他公私营机构举行会晤。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea will hold an annual consultation session with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) this week to discuss the country's overall economic situation and policies, the finance ministry said Monday. An IMF delegation, led by mission chief Corinne Delechat, is scheduled to have meetings with government ministries, including the finance, budget and industry ministries, the Bank of Korea (BOK) and other public and private institutions, according to the Ministry of Finance and Economy. The IMF team plans to hold a press conference on Nov. 17 to explain the results of the annual session after a separate meeting with Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il, it added. The IMF earlier revised up its growth forecast for Korea's economy to 3.3 percent for this year by 0.7 percentage point from its July projection amid the global semiconductor supercycle",
