   "title": "Troops Repel Terrorist Attack Along Sokoto–Gusau Road, Killed Several bandits, Rescue Civilian By: Zagazola Makama Troops of the Nigerian Ar",
   "url": "https://x.com/ZagazOlaMakama/status/2117387473668190543",
   "snippet": "Troops Repel Terrorist Attack Along Sokoto–Gusau Road, Killed Several bandits, \nRescue Civilian\n\nBy: Zagazola Makama\n\nTroops of the Nigerian Army have killed several bandits and rescued civilians after it’s repelled an attack by suspected terrorists around Kuka Mairaho Village, along the Sokoto–Gusau Main Supply Route (MSR). \n\nSecurity sources said the incident occurred at about 11:15 a.m. on November 1, 2026, when troops deployed at Forward Operating Bases (FOBs) Fangaltama and Gidan Kano were alerted to sounds of gunshots around the village.\n\nThe sources said the troops immediately mobilised to the location and engaged the terrorists, killing several fighters and forcing others to withdraw in disarray.\n\nFollowing the engagement, the troops exploited the general area and rescued one civilian.\nThe rescued victim is currently in military custody for further action.\n\nTroops continue to maintain security along the Sokoto–Gusau road and surrounding communities.",
   "body": "Troops Repel Terrorist Attack Along Sokoto–Gusau Road, Killed Several bandits, \nRescue Civilian\n\nBy: Zagazola Makama\n\nTroops of the Nigerian Army have killed several bandits and rescued civilians after it’s repelled an attack by suspected terrorists around Kuka Mairaho Village, along the Sokoto–Gusau Main Supply Route (MSR). \n\nSecurity sources said the incident occurred at about 11:15 a.m. on November 1, 2026, when troops deployed at Forward Operating Bases (FOBs) Fangaltama and Gidan Kano were alerted to sounds of gunshots around the village.\n\nThe sources said the troops immediately mobilised to the location and engaged the terrorists, killing several fighters and forcing others to withdraw in disarray.\n\nFollowing the engagement, the troops exploited the general area and rescued one civilian.\nThe rescued victim is currently in military custody for further action.\n\nTroops continue to maintain security along the Sokoto–Gusau road and surrounding communities.",
